HOW IT WORKS
What is a psychology assessment?
A psychology assessment helps you understand what’s happening with thinking, learning, attention and everyday behaviour.

It involves talking with a psychologist, completing some tasks or questions, and receiving a clear written summary.

The aim is to explain what’s going on and guide the supports, adjustments or next steps that will help at school, work or in daily life. 

