TYPES OF ASSESSMENTS
What psychological assessment might you need?
You don’t need to know which assessment you need before you contact us. That’s part of what we help you work out. We often combine assessments when the picture is complex or unclear.

ADHD assessments
Useful when focus, attention, organisation, restlessness or impulsivity affect more than one area of life.
For children, this includes input from parents, carers and teachers.
For adults, it involves exploring current patterns and earlier experiences.
Autism assessments
Useful when there are ongoing differences in communication, relationships, sensory needs, routines or daily life.
Helps build a clear picture of strengths, support needs and next steps.
Learning and literacy assessments
Useful when reading, writing, spelling or maths are harder than expected, or when schoolwork doesn’t match the effort being put in, even after extra support has been provided.
Helps identify specific learning disorders or learning differences and guides school adjustments or further support.
Cognitive and giftedness assessments
Useful when there are questions about overall learning ability, giftedness or a mismatch between ability and performance.
Helps explain how a person thinks and learns, even when reading or writing aren’t concerns.
