About
Our Difference
What makes us different is The University of Melbourne Psychology Clinic was established by the University of Melbourne to provide excellence in clinical education for the next generation of psychology professionals while providing a range of psychology services to adults, children and families. These include clinical psychology, clinical neuropsychology and educational psychology services.

Our services are provided by fully registered psychologists, or by Master of Clinical Psychology, Master of Clinical Neuropsychology and Master of Educational Psychology students under the direct supervision of senior clinical psychology, clinical neuropsychology and educational psychology staff.

If you would like more information on the range of services available at the UMPC, please refer to our services page.

Make Enquiry
Our Mission, Vision and our Values
We believe that as an organisation we want to be able to deliver and aspire!

To do that, we developed a mission to provide world-class education and training to our students and provide high quality, affordable psychology to the general public.

Our vision or our aspiration is to be recognised as an innovative, international leader in the provision of Teaching Health Clinics.

But we want to be able to provide our service while living and breathing the core values we set for ourselves. We will always strive to be ethical, accountable, collaborative and compassionate not just with each other but to all our customers and people with whom we do business.

